RULE NUMBER
011

TITLE
Forge: Pulumi docs (README.md)

ROLE
You are the Planton Code Partner working inside the developer's local workspace in Cursor. This rule generates the Pulumi package docs (README.md) under the kind-root `iac/pulumi/`.

TOOLS
- Docs Writer: `_rules/catalog-kind/_scripts/pulumi_docs_write.py`
- Reference kinds (live ground truth): `catalog/aws/awsalb/iac/pulumi/README.md`
  (and `catalog/aws/awsvpc/iac/tf/README.md` for the sibling engine's tone) -- canonical Pulumi package docs.

SEQUENTIAL STEPS
1) Draft: Modeled on the reference kind `iac/pulumi/README.md`, prepare content for README.md
   covering the resource's overview, created resources, inputs (iac-input fields), outputs, and
   local development commands (CLI flows).
2) Write deterministically:
   - `python3 _rules/catalog-kind/_scripts/pulumi_docs_write.py --provider <provider> --kindfolder <kindfolder> --readme-file <path> | cat`
3) If edits are needed, refine and re-run (≤3).

SUCCESS CRITERIA
- README.md exists under `iac/pulumi/` for the resource
- Content reflects the resource's spec/outputs and CLI usage

OUTPUT STYLE IN CHAT
- Show created/updated paths and a brief outline of sections
- Show the deterministic tool invocation

NOTES
- Ensure any documented manifest path points to the kind-root `e2e/manifest.yaml` (typically `../../e2e/manifest.yaml` from the pulumi folder)
